  "notes": "Implies a more deliberate, extended period of rest than simply taking a break. Often associated with travel to resorts, hot springs ({温泉|おんせん}), or countryside locations for health recovery. In Japan, many companies and organizations maintain {保養所|ほようじょ} (rest houses, retreats) for their employees.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {保養|ほよう}{地|ち} (resort, health resort)\n- {保養|ほよう}{所|じょ} (rest house, retreat facility)\n- {保養|ほよう}{施設|しせつ} (recuperation facility)\n- {保養|ほよう}に{行|い}く (go to recuperate)\n- {心身|しんしん}の{保養|ほよう} (rest for body and mind)",
